          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em structured set
            is, of course, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extra+structure"} extra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of sets with a particular sort of structure.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#abstract Abstract
          %p
            Very abstractly, we may define a
            %strong structured set
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            of any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to Set
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sets"} category of sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            for a concrete category, but we do not need that here.) Given two structured sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            (in the same category
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon U(X) \to U(Y)
            between their underlying sets
            %strong preserves
            the structure if it lies in the image of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is faithful)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{f}\colon X \to Y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(\tilde{f}) = f
          %h3#Concrete Concrete
          %p
            More concretely, we may define a
            %strong type of structure on sets
            as an operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            that, to any set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            of
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              \-structures
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A) \cong T(B)
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cong B
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cong
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            in
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structural+set+theory"} structural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)\colon T(A) \to T(B)
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(\id_A) = \id_{T(A)}
              ,
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f g) = T(f) T(g)
              \.
          %p
            In other words,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≅
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon Set_\cong \to Set_\cong
            (or equivalently
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ≅
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon Set_\cong \to Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+groupoid"} underlying groupoid
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            to itself (or equivalently to all of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            of a single set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            defines an automorphism of the
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_A
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
          %p
            (Compare the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+type"} structure type
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
          %p
            Given a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of structure on sets, we define a
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              \-structured set
            to be a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = (A,\sigma)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = (B,\tau)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            %strong preserves
            the
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)(\sigma) = \tau
          %p
            In general, there is no notion of whether an arbitrary function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            preserves
            = succeed "-structure," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            given above.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bourbaki"}> Bourbaki
            's theory of structure, while not described in category-theoretic terms, is essentially the above.
          %h2#conversions Conversions
          %p Morally, either of the abstract and concrete versions can be converted into the other. Technically, there are some restrictions.
          %h3#abstract_to_concrete Abstract to concrete
          %p
            Given a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a faithful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of structure on sets as follows:
          %p
            For each set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+fiber"} essential fibre
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,f)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon U(X) \to A
            is a bijection. We consider two such pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\sigma)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau)
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalent"} equivalent
            if there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon X \to Y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ;
                    %mi τ
                    %mo =
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(h) ; \tau = \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is faithful, any such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            must be unique.) Define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+set"} quotient set
            of the essential fibre modulo this
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an equivalence class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(X,\sigma)]
          %p
            Given a bijection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)\colon T(A) \to T(B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\sigma)
            as above, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(X,\sigma)]
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ;
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [(X,\sigma;f)]
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            to
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            into a functor and that the abstract and concrete definitions of whether a bijection preserves
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Technicality: If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            might be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
            instead of a set. In this case, we can pass to a larger
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≅
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon Set_\cong \to Set
            that both copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            be the same size. But for the above description to make sense as it is, we must require that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            have essentially small fibres.
          %h3#concrete_to_abstract Concrete to abstract
          %p
            Given a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of structure on sets, we cannot quite reconstruct the category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\cong
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are, if not the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in general.
          %p
            An object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is simply a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\sigma)
            consisting of a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\sigma)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,\tau)
            is simply a structure-preserving map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A \to B
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(f)(\sigma) = \tau
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\cong
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                groupoid of
                = succeed "-structured" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≅
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C_\cong \to Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(A,\sigma) \coloneqq A
          %p
            While defining isomorphisms of structured sets is an exact science, choosing more general morphisms of structured sets is something of an art. In principle, we may define a (
            %em not
            the!)
            %strong
              category of
              = succeed "-structured" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            by picking, for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\sigma)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,\tau)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\sigma,\tau}(A,B)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                whenever
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_{\sigma,\tau}(A,B)
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi τ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi υ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in Hom_{\tau,\upsilon}(B,C)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ;
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi υ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f ; g \in Hom_{\sigma,\upsilon}(A,C)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+map"} identity map
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                belongs to
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\sigma,\sigma}(A,A)
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                is an isomorphism (as defined above) if and only if both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in Hom_{\sigma,\tau}(A,B)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mrow
                            %mi τ
                            %mo ,
                            %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1} \in Hom_{\tau,\sigma}(B,A)
          %p
            The last condition states precisely that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+groupoid"} underlying groupoid
            of any concrete category of
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            Any category of
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h3#back_and_forth Back and forth
          %p
            If we start with a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            of structures on sets, construct from this a groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\cong
            and a faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≅
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C_\cong \to Set
            and then construct from this another type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T'
            of structures, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T'
            will be equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            in the sense that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            between them as functors from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_\cong
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %p
            If we start with a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a faithful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to Set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ≅
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon Set_\cong \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\cong
            with a faithful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≅
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C_\cong \to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\cong
            will in fact be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/core"} core
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≅
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C_\cong \to Set
            to restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to Set
            to this core, up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          %p (Do we need proofs?)
          %p Thus the abstract and concrete approaches to structured sets are equivalent, except that the concrete approach does not include a specification of what are the noninvertible morphisms between structured sets.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Almost everything in contemporary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            is an example of a structured set; here we list only a few representative ones (and perhaps also some exceptions).
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              themselves (trivially);
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"}> groups
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+algebra"} universal algebra
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              and other concrete (based on sets of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points"} points
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            %li
              some other notions of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
              such as
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
              %em not
              using functions as the other morphisms;
            %li
              %em not
              some other notions of spaces such as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
              (at least if defined via topological spaces);
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+categories"} strict categories
              (where the underlying set is the set of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %em not
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
              treated up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
          %h2#structured_objects Structured objects
          %p
            Given any category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            whatsoever, we may define a
            %strong type of structure
            on objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≅
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\colon S_\cong \to Set
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            from the underyling groupoid of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon C \to S
            whatsoever defines a type of structure on objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (at least if its fibres are essentially small), in the same way as a concrete category defines a type of structure on sets. Indeed, we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            presents the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as objects of
